FILED s526w2 (Opus, 2026-10-24), YAML-PP census.  LOUD (drop + the #2610 detector announces it), PRE-EXISTING.

    package TW; use Exporter "import"; our @EXPORT = qw(wl);
    sub wls (&$;$) { my ($c,$re,$d)=@_; $c->(); print "wls $re $d\n" }
    *wl = *wls;  1;
    # main: use TW; wl { 1 } qr{x}i, "desc"; print "end\n";
perl: "wls (?^i:x) desc" / end.  PCL: "statement dropped ... Missing case: [Structure::Block<{ 1 }>, Regexp]" + detector line "installed a sub with prototype (&$;$)".
Reproducer: scratch/s526w2/tw/ in the s526w2 worktree.  Test::Warn defines warning_is / warning_like exactly this way (lines 308-309), so every Test::Warn user hits it.  Static shape: a file-level `*NAME = *OTHER;` / `*NAME = \&OTHER;` whose OTHER has a declared prototype could carry the prototype over (docs/static-parse-limits-review-s512.md family; #2610 detector sees it at run time).
Rows: YAML-PP 32.cyclic-refs.t (perl 8, PCL 1).
=== DONE (s531c, 2026-11-01) ===
FIXED (commit 1e861b72) in Pl/Parser.pm `glob_sub_alias_fact`, the ONE recogniser of "code assigned to a typeglob" that the module facts walk (every load-time statement) and Parser2's pre-scan (same-file BEGIN blocks) share: it declined `*NAME = *TARGET`.  A whole-glob alias aliases the CODE slot too, so `*NAME = *TARGET;` (and `*NAME = *TARGET{CODE};`) is now the `\&TARGET` candidate: `_glob_alias_sig_info` reads TARGET's registered record, an unknown TARGET resolves nothing (as before).  The `\&TARGET` spelling already worked (probed).
Probes (scratch/s531c/tw/m.pl, m2.pl), all = perl: a use'd module's `*wl = *wls;` exported and called block-form, `*wr = \&wls`, same-file `BEGIN { *wb = *wls; *wc = *wls{CODE}; *o1 = *one }` incl. a `($)` named-unary target (`(o1 "a", "b")` is two elements).  A first draft lost `$1` to the `{CODE}` test's own match (caught by the m2 probe).
Guard: Pl/t/glob-sub-alias-01.t rows 6-7 (fail on ade297e7).  YAML-PP t/32.cyclic-refs.t (one-file run): the `warning_like { ... } qr{...}, "d";` call now parses and the #2610 detector line is gone; the file still stops after row 1, on the next cause -- Test::Builder->maybe_regex is missing from PCL's TAP layer (#4203); its *PLAN* row re-caused from #3851 to #4203 by edit.
